:: EXPERIMENT 2: PERFORM VERSION CONTROL OPERATIONS USING GIT ::

:: 1. CONFIGURE GIT (replace with your details) ::
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your-email@example.com"
git config --global --list

:: 2. INITIALIZE REPOSITORY ::
mkdir ASDD-Experiment2
cd ASDD-Experiment2
git init

:: 3. CREATE FIRST FILE ::
notepad file1.txt

:: Enter in Notepad:
This is my first Git experiment.

:: Save and close Notepad, then run:
git status
git add file1.txt
git commit -m "First commit"
git log --oneline

:: 4. MODIFY FILE AND COMMIT CHANGES ::
notepad file1.txt

:: Add this second line, then save and close:
Learning version control using Git.

:: Run:
git status
git add file1.txt
git commit -m "Updated file1"
git log --oneline

:: 5. CREATE AND SWITCH TO FEATURE BRANCH ::
git branch feature
git switch feature
git branch

:: 6. CREATE A FILE IN FEATURE BRANCH ::
notepad file2.txt

:: Enter in Notepad:
This file is created in the feature branch.

:: Save and close Notepad, then run:
git status
git add file2.txt
git commit -m "Added feature file"

:: 7. SWITCH TO MASTER AND MERGE ::
git switch master
git merge feature

:: 8. VERIFY RESULTS ::
dir
git log --oneline --all --graph
git status
git branch

:: EXPECTED FINAL STATUS ::
On branch master
nothing to commit, working tree clean

:: IMPORTANT ::
:: Run each command separately in CMD.
:: Replace the Git username and email with your own.
:: If you already created the folder, continue inside it instead of running mkdir again.
